.* WRKOBJLCK: the jobs holding or waiting for locks on one object.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=JOBCL BASETYPE='CHAR 11'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LOCKCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 14'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=THDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OBJ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OBJTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ASPDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=JOBCL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=JOBCL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=LOCK CLASS=LOCKCL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=SCOPE CLASS=LOCKCL.
:VAR NAME=THREAD CLASS=THDCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=LOCKS VARS='OPT JOB USER NUMBER LOCK STATUS SCOPE THREAD'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/OLKEYS' NAME=OLKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKOBJLCK KEYL=OLKEYS HELP=WRKOBJLCK ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Work with Object Locks
:DATA DEPTH=3.
:DATACOL WIDTH=41.
:DATAC.Object . . . . :   &OBJ.
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAC.Library  . . :     &OBJLIB.
:EDATAGRP.
:DATACOL WIDTH=39.
:DATAC.Type . . . . . :   &OBJTYPE.
:DATAC.ASP device . . :   &ASPDEV.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LOCKS ACTLEN=4.(No locks on the object)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKOBJLCK/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.4=End job
:LISTACT HELP='WRKOBJLCK/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.)'.5=Work with job
:LISTACT HELP='WRKOBJLCK/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKJOB JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) OPTION(*JOBLCK)'.8=Work with job locks
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKOBJLCK/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOB' VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT.Job
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USER' VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LOCK' VAR=LOCK USAGE=OUTPUT.Lock
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STATUS' VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT.Status
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/SCOPE' VAR=SCOPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Scope
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/THREAD' VAR=THREAD USAGE=OUTPUT.Thread
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJLCK.Work with Object Locks - Help
:P.Each job that holds a lock on the object, or waits for one, with
the lock's state. Type an option next to a job to end it or look at
it and its other locks.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/OLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJLCK/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LOCK'.Lock
:P.The lock of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SCOPE'.Scope
:P.The scope of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/THREAD'.Thread
:P.The thread of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJLCK/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.4=End job
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end job it. The End Job
(ENDJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with job
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with job it. The
Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with job locks
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with job locks it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
